Competitive Landscape
The Transition Finance and Decarbonization Lending market is increasingly dominated by a consortium of global systemically important banks (G-SIBs) that have embedded climate transition frameworks into their core lending and capital markets operations. Leading institutions are offering sustainability-linked loans, green bonds, and bespoke decarbonization lending facilities to energy-intensive sectors.
The competitive landscape is further shaped by multilateral development banks that provide concessional and blended finance instruments to de-risk private capital deployment toward hard-to-abate industries. Regional and specialist lenders are also carving out significant positions through proprietary taxonomies and data-driven underwriting models.
